# The public npm registry (registry.npmjs.org) is blocked by IT network protection on
# Microsoft locked-down laptops. Route installs through the corp package-feed proxy — an
# org-network mirror of the public npm registry — so `npm install` / `npm ci` work on any
# machine on the corp network. @microsoft/workiq lives on public npm and resolves through
# the proxy too; the scoped line also overrides a user-level ~/.npmrc that points the
# @microsoft scope at GitHub Packages.
#
# npm's default replace-registry-host=npmjs makes `npm ci` rewrite lockfile URLs whose host
# is registry.npmjs.org to this registry, so the pinned lockfile still installs via the proxy.
#
# Off the corp network? Override at install time, e.g.:
#   $env:NPM_CONFIG_REGISTRY = 'https://registry.npmjs.org'; npm install
registry=https://packagefeedproxy.microsoft.io/npm
@microsoft:registry=https://packagefeedproxy.microsoft.io/npm
